# ================================
# BLANKET SLICE, STAGE L1T: L1 (FLOW + ENERGY, FIRST-WALL FLUX) RUN IN
# PHYSICAL TIME, FOR A FLOW THAT DOES NOT SETTLE TO A STEADY STATE
#   PHYSICS  : AS blanket_L1.par (WATER 0.050 kg/s, 298.15 K; EUROFER97;
#              BC 532 1.0e5 W/m2)
#   TIME     : transient_on = 1, ONE GLOBAL TIME STEP (ilots = 0), SET BY
#              THE STABILITY LIMIT OF THE SMALLEST CELL (~4e-4 s AT h5);
#              STOPS AT end_rtime = 60 s OF PHYSICAL TIME
#   AVERAGES : export CBS3D_AVERAGE_START_TIME=20 BEFORE SUBMITTING: MEAN
#              AND RMS FIELDS FROM t = 20 s (ABOUT 3 PASSES THROUGH CHANNEL 1)
#              TO THE END, IN EVERY VTU (mean_velocity, rms_velocity,
#              mean_pressure, mean_temperature, rms_temperature, max_temperature)
#   START    : BEST FROM AN L1 FIELD (THE SOLID IS THEN NEARLY AT ITS
#              QUASI-STEADY TEMPERATURE); SEE docs/runbook SECTION 6.4b
#   OUTPUT   : ONE .pvtu EVERY 20000 STEPS (~8 s) AND AT THE END
#   CHECK    : blanket.sh check (ALSO THE TIME-AVERAGED ENERGY BALANCE)
# LINES STARTING WITH # ARE COMMENTS.
# ================================
